# Start: anywhere. End: the system carousel, awake, with nothing open --
# the state every other walk assumes.
#
# This was four B presses, which is a guess about how deep the interface
# is. B closes a dialog, a menu or a game list, but on the carousel it
# OPENS the GO TO dialog (GO TO LETTER or GO TO MANUFACTURER, by the SORT
# SYSTEMS setting; SystemView::showNavigationBar picks). So four presses
# reach the carousel from an even depth and leave GO TO open from an odd
# one: with a single dialog up -- the boot-time journey prompt, the
# RetroAchievements offer, FINISH RESTORE SETUP -- the file written to
# close things ended holding one (#85).
#
# `dismiss-dialogs` presses B until the screen repeats one it has already
# stood on. That repeat is the carousel toggling GO TO, so it stops there
# whatever the depth was, and a press that changes nothing at all is
# re-sent rather than mistaken for the repeat.
wake
dismiss-dialogs
